# CryptoNoises cron jobs (format of /etc/cron.d/*: the 6th column is the system user).
# Copy to /etc/cron.d/cryptonoises, replace /path/to/project and www-data, then enable jobs gradually:
# blockchain sync first, then analyzers and background jobs, Discord / Telegram bots last.
#
# Sync, analyze, job and notifier commands protect themselves against parallel runs, so "every minute" is safe.
# Jobs with threadIdx / threadCnt split one queue between N parallel workers - tune the counts to your hardware.
#
# This is the original schedule and it still works: every command here stops by itself after
# worker.time_limit_sec seconds (55 by default), which is what makes a one-minute tick safe.
#
# It is no longer the only option. The commands are polling workers, so they can run as long-lived processes
# instead, with only the janitors and the hourly / daily housekeeping left on a clock. The Docker stack does
# exactly that - see compose.yaml, docker/cron/schedule.cron and "Workers instead of cron" in the README. To do it
# without Docker, raise worker.time_limit_sec, run these commands under systemd units or supervisord, and keep a
# crontab holding only what docker/cron/schedule.cron holds.
#
# threadIdx / threadCnt are no longer needed for correctness: the queue claims tasks with
# SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, so plain parallel workers no longer collide. They are still accepted, so
# this file keeps working unchanged.

MAILTO=""

#=======================================================================================================================
# Tezos indexer (commands/run-tezos)
#=======================================================================================================================

# Blockchain sync (TzKT -> log tables) + removal of old log tables
*/1  *  *  *  *  www-data  /path/to/project/commands/run-tezos /blockchain/transaction/sync-new
0    *  *  *  *  www-data  /path/to/project/commands/run-tezos /blockchain/transaction/cleanup offset=50000

*/1  *  *  *  *  www-data  /path/to/project/commands/run-tezos /blockchain/bigmap-updates/sync-new
*/1  *  *  *  *  www-data  /path/to/project/commands/run-tezos /blockchain/bigmap-updates/sync-check thread-id=1 offset=2     # re-check blocks ~1 min back
*/1  *  *  *  *  www-data  /path/to/project/commands/run-tezos /blockchain/bigmap-updates/sync-check thread-id=2 offset=120   # re-check blocks ~1 hour back
0    *  *  *  *  www-data  /path/to/project/commands/run-tezos /blockchain/bigmap-updates/cleanup offset=50000

# Analyzers
*/1  *  *  *  *  www-data  /path/to/project/commands/run-tezos /analyze/transactions/new
*/1  *  *  *  *  www-data  /path/to/project/commands/run-tezos /analyze/bigmap-updates/new limit=50000

# Background jobs (queues)
*/1  *  *  *  *  www-data  /path/to/project/commands/run-tezos /jobs/exec jobId=sync-contracts-metadata threadIdx=0 threadCnt=4
*/1  *  *  *  *  www-data  /path/to/project/commands/run-tezos /jobs/exec jobId=sync-contracts-metadata threadIdx=1 threadCnt=4
